WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:02.585
♪♪♪
- Today on "Sneak This,"
can't believe we got him.

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:04.587
Floyd the mailman.
[Bell dinging, applause]
♪♪♪

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.722
- Gentlemen.
- Have you seen anybody wear
the post office Air Force 1s?

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:15.390
- What? There's such a thing?

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.143
- Yeah, can we get—
- Yeah, throw 'em up right there.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:18.935
- Can we throw 'em up?

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:21.646
- You might not be aware of
this, but in the sneaker world,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.106
you're basically Santa Claus.
[Sound of water running]

00:00:23.898 --> 00:00:24.399
- Oh yeah, man.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:25.775
I've thought I've been Santa
Claus for a long time now,

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:28.028
to be honest with you.
The guy's coming to your door, man.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.362
Leave me a plate of cookies, you know?

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.490
- What kind of shoes
do you wear as a mailman?

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:33.783
- Uh, the New Balance.
[Crowd reaction sound]

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.410
They have a work series, like a 626.

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:39.873
- When you see our house, are there any
signs that a sneakerhead lives there?

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:40.623
- Sure.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:43.835
You know, you see the same—those boxes
constantly coming like that, come in and out.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.670
I mean, I pretty much can tell
what's coming through and what's

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.173
coming into the mail. Some of those
boxes with the black bags,

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:49.257
you know there's a magazine in there.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.342
There's only one magazine
they deliver in a black bag.
[Whispering:] Pornography.

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:58.725
- Whenever you're shipping a pair of
sneakers, they always ask you,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.226
how much do you want to insure these for?

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:02.062
So that's why we're playing the game

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:05.273
"How much would you [bell dings]
insure these sneakers for?" [bell dings]

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:07.859
- I wouldn't pay more than $120 for those.
- How much are these? $25,000?
[Buzzer]

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:12.322
- [Laughing] Get out.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:13.031
Are you serious?
- Yeah.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:20.622
- That's not the same shoe?
- It's definitely different.
- How much you insuring these for?
- Two and a quarter.
- Two and a quarter?
- Two hundred and twenty five.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:22.665
- Dollars.
- These are going for like $8,000.
[Buzzer]

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.125
- OK, uh, $450?

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:27.879
- Times three.
[Buzzer]

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:31.424
- $2,250.
- Like $12K.
[Buzzer]
- $375.
- $20,000.
[Buzzer]

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:35.136
- The New Balance is one of
my favorite brands. They're always

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:36.304
reasonably priced for the working man.

00:01:36.304 --> 00:01:41.434
I'd say $295.
- Pretty reasonable. These are $450.
[Crowd reaction sound]

00:01:41.851 --> 00:01:46.815
Finally, if you could give one piece of
advice for the sneakerheads out there

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:48.775
in the world, what would you tell them?

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.862
- Get to know your mailman
- Fucker!
- Get to know your mailman, kids.
♪♪♪

